  "section_notes": "S1 imposes strict 24-hour reporting for all listed incidents and 72-hour customer notice. S2 sets a 55°C test and 5% limit for new models, with an open-ended corrective-action path for existing models and no public per-model publication. S3 delays new-unit shut-off to 24 months and retrofit to 72 months; S4 requires suppression by 36 months; S5 uses an 8/100k trigger for notification/assessment but leaves recall to regulator discretion."
